<title>UK: Sumitomo Bank buys back 2004 convertible.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Bank buys back 2004 convertible.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Bank said on Wednesday it had purchased over 95 percent of its $300 million 3.125 percent convertible bonds maturing on March 31, 2004. Its tender offer, announced on October 30, expired on Tuesday and all bonds repurchased would be cancelled, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Earlier Sumitomo said that the offer was designed to strengthen its financial condition by trimming interest rate payments as well as its total debt.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers International acted as exclusive dealer manager on the offer.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7658</p>
